  "term": "flexibilitas cerea",
  "definition": "Flexibilitas cerea is a historical term for a catatonic sign in which, if a person’s resistance is slight or can be overcome, their limbs can be placed and left in unusual or uncomfortable positions. It refers to this waxy-seeming maintenance of an imposed posture.",
